.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS inventory
.PP
.I List UEFI boot entries and classify each (live, dangling, duplicate, dead\-OS)
.PP
.B Category:
Diagnostics
.br
.B Maturity:
draft
.PP
.B SYNTAX
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram inventory [\-\-efidisk FILE] [\-\-json]
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B ARGUMENTS
.PP
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-\-efidisk FILE
Inspect an offline efidisk/OVMF_VARS image instead of live efivarfs
.RE
.PP
.B EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram inventory
lamboot\-nvram inventory \-\-efidisk /dev/zvol/AB/vm\-129\-disk\-1 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B NOTES
.PP
.RS 4
Resolves each Boot#### against present partitions. Reads live efivarfs (unprivileged) or, with \-\-efidisk, an offline vars image via virt\-fw\-vars.
.RE
.PP
.B OFFLINE:
Yes \- supports \fB\-\-offline\fR \fIDISK\fR
.br
.B PRIVILEGE:
Runs unprivileged
.PP
.B SEE ALSO
.PP
.RS 4
clean
.RE
.PP
.B DOCUMENTATION URL
.PP
.RS 4
.UR https://github.com/lamco-admin/lamboot-tools
.UE
.RE
.PP
.SS clean
.PP
.I Remove stale UEFI boot entries (dry\-run by default)
.PP
.B Category:
Maintenance
.br
.B Maturity:
draft
.PP
.B SYNTAX
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram clean [\-\-apply] [\-\-category CAT ...] [\-\-exclude CAT ...] [\-\-efidisk FILE] [\-\-backup\-dir DIR] [\-\-json]
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B ARGUMENTS
.PP
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually delete entries (default: preview only)
.TP
.B \-\-category CAT
dangling 
.TP
.B  duplicate 
 duplicate 
.TP
.B  dead\-os 
 dead\-os 
.TP
.B  orphan\-bootorder (repeatable; default
 all)
.TP
.B \-\-exclude CAT
Skip a category (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-efidisk FILE
Operate on an offline efidisk image (inventory/preview; apply is live\-only)
.TP
.B \-\-backup\-dir DIR
Where to export the pre\-change NVRAM
.RE
.PP
.B EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram clean
sudo lamboot\-nvram clean \-\-category duplicate \-\-apply
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B NOTES
.PP
.RS 4
NEVER removes BootCurrent or the default (BootOrder head). Backs up via efibootmgr \-v before \-\-apply; reverse with \'lamboot\-nvram restore\'. Logs every action to /var/log/lamboot/.
.RE
.PP
.B OFFLINE:
Yes \- supports \fB\-\-offline\fR \fIDISK\fR
.br
.B PRIVILEGE:
Requires root (sudo)
.PP
.B SEE ALSO
.PP
.RS 4
inventory,restore
.RE
.PP
.B DOCUMENTATION URL
.PP
.RS 4
.UR https://github.com/lamco-admin/lamboot-tools
.UE
.RE
.PP
.SS restore
.PP
.I Re\-create boot entries removed by a previous clean (from its backup)
.PP
.B Category:
Maintenance
.br
.B Maturity:
draft
.PP
.B SYNTAX
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram restore [\-\-apply] [\-\-backup\-dir DIR] [\-\-json]
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B ARGUMENTS
.PP
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually re\-create entries (default: preview only)
.TP
.B \-\-backup\-dir DIR
Backup to restore from (default: most recent /var/backups/lamboot\-{nvram,doctor}\-*)
.RE
.PP
.B EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lamboot\-nvram restore
sudo lamboot\-nvram restore \-\-apply
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B NOTES
.PP
.RS 4
Reads the backup\'s efibootmgr.pre.txt, re\-creates any entry present then but missing now (efibootmgr \-c, resolving the disk from the partition UUID). Idempotent.
.RE
.PP
.B OFFLINE:
No \- requires online system
.br
.B PRIVILEGE:
Requires root (sudo)
.PP
.B SEE ALSO
.PP
.RS 4
clean
.RE
.PP
.B DOCUMENTATION URL
.PP
.RS 4
.UR https://github.com/lamco-admin/lamboot-tools
.UE
.RE
.PP
